# A rubric asked about one message between coding agents that share a
# repository: what it needs from the agent it is addressed to. The state is
# the message, `{"subject": ..., "body": ...}`.
#
# Three Nouls rather than one Choice, because the messages are multi-label:
# "landed (054fc51), gate please, and one thing fleet.rs should know" asks
# for something AND warns about something. A Choice over {status, request,
# warning} would have to drop one of the two.
#
# The answers rank and escalate; they never hide. In the fleets these cases
# come from, the message that mattered was a small minority that no rule
# could predict, so a gate that drops a message drops that one too.
apiVersion: jud/v1
kind: Rubric
metadata:
  name: agent-mail
  minor: 3
  version: 1
  description: >-
    What a message between coding agents needs from its recipient: an action,
    attention to something that broke, or nothing beyond knowing the work is done.
spec:
  questions:
    needs_action:
      type: noul
      instructions: >-
        Does `body` (under `subject`) ask its recipient to do something: decide,
        approve, answer, run a check, make an edit, or check their own work?
      criteria:
        true: a question, a request for approval or a decision, "gate please", an edit to make, "check your work"
        false: a report or an answer that leaves the recipient nothing to do, including "no action needed"
    breaks_something:
      type: noul
      instructions: >-
        Does `body` (under `subject`) warn its recipient that something they own
        or rely on is broken, lost, changed or wrong: a reverted or overwritten
        change, an interface that changed under them, a failing build or check,
        a defect in their file, a premise that does not hold?
      criteria:
        true: a revert, an overwrite, a changed contract, a red build or gate, a defect, a wrong assumption
        false: news that leaves everything the recipient relies on as it was
    status_only:
      type: noul
      instructions: >-
        Is `body` (under `subject`) only a report that work is done or under way,
        with nothing the recipient must do and nothing they must know beyond that?
      criteria:
        true: started, done, landed, acknowledged, with no request, no warning and no finding
        false: carries a request, a warning, a decision or a finding the recipient needs

  # Read off 33 cases with no held-out set: a starting point to re-tune on a
  # larger corpus, not a measured bar. The order the probabilities put the
  # messages in is the stronger result (area under the ROC curve 0.90, 0.89
  # and 0.97 on these recordings); the 0.5 default reads breaks_something as
  # yes for 25 of 33 messages.
  policy:
    needs_action:
      threshold: 0.45
      note: best F1 on 33 labelled cases; 0.96 recall
    breaks_something:
      threshold: 0.75
      note: best F1 on 33 labelled cases; 0.93 recall, 0.68 precision. A missed warning costs more than a glance
    status_only:
      threshold: 0.15
      note: best F1 on 33 labelled cases; the model never puts a status report above 0.5

  tuning:
    cases: sha256:aefbd6d9f9611a03753f422fb9d1aeac4125d8ad232c1849cacc5067fef64245
    model: jev-1.13.0
    server: https://api.typesafe.ai
    tuned_at: 2026-10-14T04:20:54Z
    labelled:
      needs_action: 33
      breaks_something: 33
      status_only: 33
